paraphrase:
A row of \(10\) adjacent squares is drawn below, with a diagonal in each square running from its bottom-left vertex to its top-right vertex. Starting at the bottom-left corner \(A\), a bug travels along the drawn segments between vertices to reach the top-right corner \(B\). It may not use any segment more than once, and every move along a horizontal or diagonal segment must be from left to right. The thick segments illustrate one permitted route.

If \(N\) denotes the total number of permitted paths from \(A\) to \(B\), determine \(\sqrt{N}\).

[asy]
size(12cm);
draw((0, 0)--(0, 1));
for (int i = 0; i <= 9; i += 1)
{
draw((i, 1)--(i + 1, 1)--(i + 1, 0)--(i, 0)--(i + 1, 1));
}
draw((0, 0)--(0, 1)--(2, 1)--(2, 0)--(3, 1)--(3, 0)--(4, 1)--(4, 0)--(5, 0)--(5, 1)--(6, 1)--(6, 0)--(7, 1)--(8, 1)--(8, 0)--(10, 0)--(10, 1), red + linewidth(2));
label("$A$", (0, 0), dir(180));
label("$B$", (10, 1), dir(0));
[/asy]

Find the exact value of
\[
\int_{0}^{1}
\frac{\arctan\!\left(\sqrt{\frac{2+x^2}{4+x^2}}\right)}
{(1+x^2)\sqrt{2+x^2}}\,dx.
\]
